    "positionStepJulianDays": 1,
    "interpolation": "cubic-hermite-cartesian-with-central-difference-tangents",
    "orbitSamplesPerPlanet": 192,
    "orbitReferenceJulianDate": 2451545,
    "note": "One-Julian-day keyframes from VSOP87A (heliocentric rectangular, ecliptic and equinox J2000; the earlier build used VSOP87C, which is referred to the ecliptic of date and drifted about 50 arcseconds a year from the J2000 star frame). The runtime interpolates with cubic Hermite segments whose tangents are central differences, removing the up-to-6,000 km chord error of linear interpolation. Orbit paths are representative display guides sampled across one nominal period about J2000 and are not osculating elements."
  },
